; Bona — timer for bona-ig-publish.service.
;
; Every 15 minutes from 17:00 to 23:45 Asia/Riyadh. The zone is written INTO the calendar
; expression (systemd >= 240 accepts it), so the schedule holds even if this machine's zone
; changes; `timedatectl` on this box is Asia/Riyadh already. Check the next elapse with
;   systemd-analyze calendar "*-*-* 17..23:00/15 Asia/Riyadh"
;
; Why that window: every slot in the calendar sits in it (stories 17:15, feed 20:30, 3D-tour
; stories 21:05, the launch grid 17:30 → 20:10) and the service's --grace 3 h means a run
; missed for any reason is caught by a later one the same evening.
; Grace never exceeds the window: the last tick is 23:45 and the latest slot (21:05) + 3 h
; lapses at 00:05, so nothing is "still due" when the timer wakes the next day. (A 6 h grace
; left 21:05 valid until 03:05 with no tick to serve it — and a boot-time catch-up would have
; posted it at 02:00.) The publisher also refuses to post outside 17:00–23:59 KSA
; (deferred:quiet-hours) whatever the grace says.
; Persistent=true: if the box was off at a tick, run once at the next boot. Inside the window
; that catches up on the evening; outside it the quiet-hours guard makes it a no-op.

[Unit]
Description=Bona — Instagram publisher, every 15 min 17:00–23:59 KSA

[Timer]
OnCalendar=*-*-* 17..23:00/15 Asia/Riyadh
Persistent=true
AccuracySec=30s
Unit=bona-ig-publish.service

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
